  "worked_solution": "The table shows probabilities in the form $P(X\\ge x).$ So first, we express the desired probability in this form:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(X\\ge x) & =1-P(X\\le x) \\\\  & =1-0.95 \\\\  & =0.05\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, since $X∼{T}_{15},$ we focus on the row of the table that corresponds to $k=15.$\n\n| $k∖p$ | $0.100$ | $0.050$ | $0.025$ | $0.010$ | $0.005$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $15$ | $1.341$ | $1.753$ | $2.131$ | $2.602$ | $2.947$ |\n| $16$ | $1.337$ | $1.746$ | $2.120$ | $2.583$ | $2.921$ |\n| $17$ | $1.333$ | $1.740$ | $2.110$ | $2.567$ | $2.898$ |\n\nFrom this row, we see that\n\n$$\nP(X\\ge 1.753)=0.050.\n$$\n\nTherefore, our answer is $x=1.753.$",
